    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710a-114">

                <pb facs="0601" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">July 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 316. For Ambassador Winant[.] London’s
                    44360 July 24<anchor n="2" xml:id="d710a-114-f1"/> received. Strang told Mosely
                    today FonOff has full authority instruct Hood accept Soviet final paragraph
                    covering report on French zone.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d710a-114-f2"/> Meanwhile
                    US, UK and French commanders have agreed on French area in Berlin.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d710a-114-f3"/> Strang obviously does not understand FonOff
                    delay.</p>
                <p>Gousev told Mosely today instructions sent Saksin yesterday to accept title of
                    agreement on additional requirements with inclusion of words “to be
                    imposed.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710a-114-f1" n="2" xml:id="d710a-114-f1-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1031">Document No. 1031</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >post</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-114-f2" n="3" xml:id="d710a-114-f2-content">
                <p>Cf. the following passage in a personal letter from Mosely, dated at Babelsberg
                    July 24, to E. Allan Lightner, Jr., Secretary of the United States Delegation to
                    the European Advisory Commission (file No. 740.00119 Control (Germany)/7–2445):
                    “Strang has just told me that instructions were sent to Hood on July 22 to
                    accept the Soviet formula for the final sentence of the report. The British
                    agree that the exact definition of the French sector should be done by military
                    agreement and need not be incorporated into the EAC Agreement.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-114-f3" n="4" xml:id="d710a-114-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d1028">document No. 1028</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
